[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3105725987","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3105725987","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3105725987,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65HZ4j","user":{"login":"JonathanHaws","id":108207472,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnMdcA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108207472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws","html_url":"https://github.com/JonathanHaws","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T05:20:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T05:20:46Z","body":"Also another issue I found with having to pause the tree is making audio pause is a lot more tedious to do","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3105725987/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3109460411","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3109460411","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3109460411,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65Vpm7","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T17:10:45Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T17:11:12Z","body":"I don't know how heavily `Engine.time_scale = 0` is tested, but I'm not sure it's meant to be used as a replacement for pausing. Many other engines also don't support using a time scale of `0` and require at least `0.001` or something.\n\ncc @lawnjelly as he might have some insight on this.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3109460411/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110014017","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3110014017","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3110014017,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65XwxB","user":{"login":"JonathanHaws","id":108207472,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnMdcA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108207472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws","html_url":"https://github.com/JonathanHaws","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T20:17:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T20:17:00Z","body":"Why do other engines not support it? Is their some technical reason? I dont see how an early return on move_and_slide() would cause issues? At the very least should throw something like 'Physics error: Cannot simulate movement when Engine.time_scale is 0\"\nAnd if you can check for that why not also just skip? \n\nSilently changing data in unpredictable ways makes bugs caused by this difficult to isolate and track down","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110014017/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110151355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3110151355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3110151355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65YSS7","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T20:57:06Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T20:57:06Z","body":"Unity [seems to support](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.1/Documentation/ScriptReference/Time-timeScale.html) `Time.timeScale` set to `0`.\n\n>When timeScale is set to zero your application acts as if paused if all your functions are frame rate independent. Negative values are ignored.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110151355/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110183522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3110183522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3110183522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65YaJi","user":{"login":"JonathanHaws","id":108207472,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnMdcA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108207472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws","html_url":"https://github.com/JonathanHaws","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JonathanHaws/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T21:10:37Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T21:10:37Z","body":"This is how I think it should work! I dont see why Godot couldn't work in same way. I don't imagine it would be that costly for performance either? \n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110183522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110219436","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3110219436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3110219436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65Yi6s","user":{"login":"Changryy","id":35406747,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NDA2NzQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35406747?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy","html_url":"https://github.com/Changryy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Changryy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T21:26:44Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T21:26:44Z","body":"I agree with Calinou that if the intention is to pause the game the [pause](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/pausing_games.html) feature is better suited for that purpose, but `time_scale` set to 0 should not break physics like this regardless.\n\nI see 2 solutions for this issue:\n1. Physics should be paused when `time_scale` is 0. You can still get collision data, but physics bodies dont move. This is the optimal solution in my opinion.\n2. It should be documented that `time_scale` 0 is not supported. We could optionally prevent people from setting `time_scale` to 0 to avoid bugs like these.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110219436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3111966840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108879#issuecomment-3111966840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108879","id":3111966840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65fNh4","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-24T05:00:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T05:00:00Z","body":"> cc @lawnjelly as he might have some insight on this.\n\nNo particular expert here, but I also think the engine should be tolerant of 0 timescale (and indeed maybe switch some systems off possibly, but not super necessary). If code produces NaN with 0 timescale, it's duff code imo, and should have checks for things like divide by zero.\n\nI also think engines should support 0 scale too (I was never sure of the way Godot stores key rotations / scales as only a basis) but that's a whole other topic.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3111966840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]